Usage: unidoc [argument ...]

  Arguments may be options or file and directory names and are processed
  from left to right.  Some options remain in effect from the
  point they appear until negated by a later option.  Other
  options affect all files.  At least one directory or Unicon source
  file name must appear as an argument.

Options:

--resolve    - Try to resolve entities referenced in any
               of the following named source files.

--noresolve  - Don't try to resolve entities referenced in
               any of the following named source files. (default)

--targetDir=DIR - Put the generated HTML documents in DIR
                  (DIR defaults to "./htmlDoc/"

--sourcePath=DIRLIST - also look in DIRLIST for source files

--indexFile=FILE - Name the base index file FILE.
                  (FILE defaults to "index.html"

--title=TITLE    - Use TITLE as the title for output
                  (TITLE defaults to "Generated Documentation"
--linkSrc    - Try to include links back to the source code.
                  (Note: can be tricked if multiple source files
                   have the same name!)

--nolinkSrc  - Don't include links to the source code (default).
